1. She experiences anxiety, especially when being outside or in crowds. (Verbatim: "being outside it's really difficult for me... anxiety is heckin real and yeah well it's heckin scary like people are scary")
2. She finds it easier to manage her anxiety when she is with her dog. (Verbatim: "i feel when i go out i'm not as anxious when i have my dog... dog definitely helps a lot")
3. She prioritizes her dog’s safety over her own when walking near roads. (Verbatim: "if there's not enough room dog gets to stay on the pavement i walk on the road for a little bit")
4. She has a strong preference for organized environments, noting she felt less stress in Japan due to orderly pedestrian flow. (Verbatim: "in japan everyone naturally tries to make streams of like one everyone going one way... it felt organized")
5. She has experienced being physically bumped into or pushed by people while walking, even when trying to be cautious. (Verbatim: "there have been times where i've been walking and like i'll be walking along the pavement... and then i just get knocked into the road")
6. She identifies as an overthinker, especially in public, analyzing people's movement paths to avoid collisions. (Verbatim: "i'm definitely an overthinker when i'm out so i'm like trying to analyze everybody's path")
7. She dislikes being the imposter in games like Among Us because it makes her anxious and she doesn’t like lying or pretending. (Verbatim: "i don't like being imposter... it's scary and i don't want to lie")
8. She has lived in or visited both Japan and England, and has observed cultural differences in walking behavior. (Verbatim: "when i was in japan japan wasn't too bad compared to england like when i went into the city the other day")
9. She attended school in England, where she also experienced being pushed or knocked around in crowded areas. (Verbatim: "even at like school oh gosh he's getting knocked on the wall like")
10. She struggles with advice like “walk with confidence” because it hasn’t worked for her in practice. (Verbatim: "i've tried to walk with confidence i just get i just get pushed... you can't walk with confidence and i can't even when i'm walking without confidence i still get pushed") [end of text]



